# Prettier reads only the ignore files it is handed, and `--ignore-path`
# replaces its defaults — so anything ignored by a *nested* .gitignore is
# invisible to it. That is not hypothetical: `cap sync` copies the exported web
# bundle and its config into apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/assets, which
# apps/mobile/android/.gitignore covers, and `pnpm format:check` then failed on
# thousands of generated chunks after every Android build while a clean checkout
# passed. The two files disagreeing is the whole bug, so this repeats those
# paths where prettier can see them.

# Generated native payloads: the synced web bundle plus the Capacitor config and
# plugin manifest that `cap sync` writes next to it.
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/assets/
apps/mobile/ios/App/App/public/

# Static exports.
apps/*/out/
